{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding","id":1171195,"title":"Lunar dragon-blooded breeding?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-28T04:10:33-08:00","id":1171195,"title":"Lunar dragon-blooded breeding?","content":"So I was thinking: If a Lunar can shapeshift into animal X, breed in that form to produce a superior version of animal X with a few choice mutations...<br /> <br /> ...why not have a lunar shapeshift into the form of a dragonblooded human with very pure dragonblood and then sire a legion of surprisingly potent DBs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T04:35:54-08:00","id":1171200,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately (well, maybe fortunately for the setting), it doesn't work.<br /> Lunars can take the form of Dragonblood, but they don't gain the Dragonblood exaltation. So just as they don't gain the Dragonblood's charms, they don't gain the Dragonblood's ability to create Dragonblooded kids. They just don't have the magic necessary.<br /> <br /> I'm sure some Lunars have tried though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T04:39:42-08:00","id":1171201,"title":"","content":"You know, I was writing out a post about the multi-faceted practical logistic and social difficulties of this endeavour, but then it struck me that I was thinking about everything using the old rules.<br /> <br /> \u200bNobody can father thousands of Dragon Blooded, because your progenitive Essence gets used up after just one of them, and takes several years to regenerate.<br /> <br /> Any question about whether or not a Lunar can even approximate that is largely irrelevant, because they still can't do better than it.<br /> <br /> Simple.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T04:45:26-08:00","id":1171202,"title":"","content":"My In-Character Reason: because the way Lunars express their essence does not change with their form. A Lunar who turns into an owl is a still a lunar, able to use lunar charms and liable to reproduce some kind of beastmen instead of normal owls. A Lunar who turns into another human, then, even if it's a human who was Dragonblooded... will still be a lunar, and liable to reproduce lunar-essence-infused humans instead of Dragonblooded humans.<br /> <br /> My Out-of-Character Reason: Because that is hax OP bullshit, and I was <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/273667-child-bearing-obligations-of-the-scarlet-dynasty?p=273832#post273832\">already predisposed</a> to nix any plan that had the words &quot;Lunar&quot; and &quot;Breeding&quot; in it, because those are invariably skeezy and diminish the personhood of every character involved besides the plan's initiator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T04:59:53-08:00","id":1171205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171201#post1171201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I was writing out a post about the multi-faceted practical logistic and social difficulties of this endeavour, but then it struck me that I was thinking about everything using the old rules.<br /> <br /> \u200bNobody can father thousands of Dragon Blooded, because your progenitive Essence gets used up after just one of them, and takes several years to regenerate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually missed the word &quot;legion&quot;, so didn't think of that. I was just thinking of them having a handful of DB kids. But you're right.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But you've also reminded me that, well, generally, who wants to give birth to tons of kids? Some women, yeah, but not most.<br /> <br /> <br /> We have a Lunar PC who can cut her pregnancy to 3 months with charms. So far she's had... 1 kid. Which was an accident. I think he's like 1.5 years old now? <br /> <br /> <br /> It's not like being able to have 1 or 2 kids a year is useful for her. I mean, he might be a Lunar-blooded. Or Solar-blooded. But he's less than 2. His primary role in the party is burping, and occasionally having kidnap attempts against him (I gave him a bear familiar, so he hasn't actually been kidnapped yet). She has to find a babysitter whenever we go on an adventure. Sometimes she just brings him with us, then complains a lot that this isn't a suitable adventure for a 1 year old.<br /> <br /> She could have, like 10 Lunar-blooded kids I guess. And in 20 years that'd be useful. Until then she'd have to care for them.<br /> Or she could just make her husband the Pharoah and have a whole country (which already has a handful of experienced Dragonblood) to obey her (she's got him into 2nd in line for the throne, which is pretty good considering he's a common soldier's orphan). Much easier. In fact, she's already got one Dragonblood on side (her husband's third wife), without having to wait 20 years.<br /> <br /> So even if a Lunar could have DB kids, I don't think they'd try to have hundreds of them. That'd take a hundred years of doing very little. There's much less laborious (literally) ways to get an army of Dragonblood than produce themselves.<br /> <br /> Not to mention sorcerers can summon up magical servants anyway...<br /> <br /> I mean, what soldier-king ever said &quot;I need an army of dedicated warriors. I shall do this by having tons of kids!&quot; It's just a bit bizarre.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T05:50:51-08:00","id":1171211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171205#post1171205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> But you've also reminded me that, well, generally, who wants to give birth to tons of kids? Some women, yeah, but not most.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, webkilla did say <i>sire</i> a legion, and sire is a noun and verb referring to fathers.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe whole narrative of a lone Dragon Blood breeding an army from himself has always been kind of inherently patriarchal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, what soldier-king ever said &quot;I need an army of dedicated warriors. I shall do this by having tons of kids!&quot; It's just a bit bizarre.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, there are two aspects to this. One is that, given the lack of hereditary supernatural powers in real life, there's not really an advantage to breeding an army of your own children rather than just drawing upon somebody else's, at least in terms of their fighting strength. In settings where such power is hereditary, it would make a measure of sense to attempt creating your master race or army in that manner, if the ethical concerns didn't move you. You'd still probably run into the issue of providing for and managing them, though.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe other aspect is that it's worth pointing out that there have been many monarchs in history who did, indeed, have dozens or even more than a hundred children. There hasn't often been a practical element to it, more often just being a logical conclusion of the status symbol of having a large number of wives and/or consorts, although there are some times when the large number of children themselves is also a status symbol, and some systems in which the lack of simple primogeniture includes a kind of notion of having a large number of children so that you can select the best successor, rather than trusting to the luck of the draw from the two or three you have that might turn out to be unsuitable.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's just, given the differences in roles for creating children, it's just plain easier for a man to father lots of children than it is for a woman. I'd argue that it's a foundational element of patriarchy, how having children is at least biologically a lot easier on men (assuming no health or fertility problems).<br /> <br /> \u200bFrom this point, I can actually admit a bit of surprise, and relief, that it was never really an example cited by people who were really big on the idea of breeding an army, or even just fixated on maximizing the higher breeding in a general sense, as it really would have been difficult to dispute on their terms. I mean, the agency of Dragon Blooded women could probably serve as an effective counter argument if anybody had ever suggested that the setup that the Manual gave to the original Terrestrial Exalted was how they worked all the time, but it would kind of rub up unpleasantly against some ideas of the mortal population of the world. At the very least, it's the kind of thing that kind of hung down on the neck of taking assertions that the Realm had a matriarchal bias seriously.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe adjustment with the idea that, when it comes to inheriting their power, Dragon Blooded of any gender are basically dealing with a kind of spiritual ovulation cycle relieves a lot of this significantly.<br /> <br /> .... Oh <i>that's</i> why there would be a stronger stigma against extramarital children for the men; they're expending (and possibly wasting) the progenitive Essence that they probably implicitly or explicitly owe to their wife.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo yeah, a few things working against it now.<br /> <br /> \u200bBy the way, webkilla, there's nothing about this setup now that would make the resulting Dragon Blooded particularly potent, surprising or otherwise; it's been made clear that Breeding isn't going to include things like extra motes or being the prerequisite to especially powerful Charms anymore. If you had a lot of well bred Exalted, they would be a bit better for making more well bred Exalted, but as this is all alluding to, not many more of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T07:36:57-08:00","id":1171229,"title":"","content":"In Third Edition, Lunar Exalted can only take the Heart's Blood of animals and other humans.<br /> <br /> Obviously, Heart's Blood does not include any Exaltations, Celestial or Terrestrial.<br /> <br /> Even if Heart's Blood allowed a Lunar to take on a mortals inherited Blood of the Dragons which did not ignite into an Exaltation, this wouldn't give the Lunar any better chances of siring a full-on Terrestrial Exalt than if the Lunar had already been born with the Blood of the Dragons herself.<br /> <br /> Neither can a Lunar use Heart's Blood stolen from a victim she left alive to siphon away his progenitive potential, any more than she could use that link to steal his motes or thoughts.<br /> <br /> (A willing Dragon-Blood might be able to allow the Lunar act as a surrogate, because at that point, the Lunar is acting as an extension of the Dragon-Blood, rather than a thief.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T08:10:57-08:00","id":1171236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding#post1171195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was thinking: If a Lunar can shapeshift into animal X, breed in that form to produce a superior version of animal X with a few choice mutations...<br /> <br /> ...why not have a lunar shapeshift into the form of a dragonblooded human with very pure dragonblood and then sire a legion of surprisingly potent DBs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because why would they? This setup, minus the Lunars, already exists in Creation: it's called the Realm, and so far the Lunars haven't had a great experience with it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T18:06:52-08:00","id":1171384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171201#post1171201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody can father thousands of Dragon Blooded, because your progenitive Essence gets used up after just one of them, and takes several years to regenerate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pardon me, but what the Fokuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21242-charonferryman","name":"CharonFerryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T18:32:19-08:00","id":1171390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171202#post1171202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Out-of-Character Reason: Because that is hax OP bullshit, and I was <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/273667-child-bearing-obligations-of-the-scarlet-dynasty?p=273832#post273832\">already predisposed</a> to nix any plan that had the words &quot;Lunar&quot; and &quot;Breeding&quot; in it, because those are invariably skeezy and diminish the personhood of every character involved besides the plan's initiator.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might be off-topic, but one of my characters is actually the result of a Lunar's breeding plan: a tyrant lizard beastman. He Exalted as a Dawn, and has since tried to refine himself and abandon his father's plans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Teller of Tales, and the Weaver of Dreams<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Behold! My 2e characters.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","name":"Voyd211","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13327_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T18:39:56-08:00","id":1171396,"title":"","content":"Still, I'm interested to know what sort of Lunar Charms we might see for siring or bearing beastfolk and/or &quot;Moon-touched&quot; children, and for investing chosen priests and children with authority and power, in a reflection of the Solar Presence Charms for choosing and empowering servants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T19:06:11-08:00","id":1171410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171396#post1171396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, I'm interested to know what sort of Lunar Charms we might see for siring or bearing beastfolk and/or &quot;Moon-touched&quot; children, and for investing chosen priests and children with authority and power, in a reflection of the Solar Presence Charms for choosing and empowering servants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honest question: how would this ever work in actual play? Are timeskips of multiple decades really all that frequent in Exalted chronicles? My personal experience is that real downtime is rare and mostly means either a few days to a few weeks in transit (depending mainly on whether someone took Stormwind Rider) or maybe a few months for the season to change, so I'd think that the story would be largely <i>over </i>by the time you see any kind of return on investment for these Charms. Maybe it could work if the group starts out playing older Lunars, but 1) again, IME, that rarely happens, and 2) it would only work for justifying merits purchased at chargen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T19:20:37-08:00","id":1171415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CharonFerryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171384#post1171384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pardon me, but what the Fokuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's something the devs explained thoroughly; even Dragon-Blooded can't just crank out hundreds of Dragon-Blooded babies. The best chances they have at their kids Exalting is when there's years and years between conceiving said kids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T19:25:56-08:00","id":1171418,"title":"","content":"It depends on the chronicle and the events at hand. I mean if you're in the middle of stuff then yeah not likely to happen, but you're situated, there's nothing imperative, and the rest of the group is fine with it, then yeah 20 years later, &quot;Alright guys I made a new diaklave and it isn't actively trying to kill me. What have you been up to?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T19:37:11-08:00","id":1171420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171211#post1171211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bWell, webkilla did say <i>sire</i> a legion, and sire is a noun and verb referring to fathers.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe whole narrative of a lone Dragon Blood breeding an army from himself has always been kind of inherently patriarchal.</div> </div> </div> </div>New Lunar Charm: Efficacious Seahorse Imitation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T21:39:34-08:00","id":1171448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171415#post1171415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's something the devs explained thoroughly; even Dragon-Blooded can't just crank out hundreds of Dragon-Blooded babies. The best chances they have at their kids Exalting is when there's years and years between conceiving said kids.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true. Of course, just to point out it's also something that while the readers know about, might not be something that the people of Creation are entirely familiar with. I suspect that there are probably a few Dragon Blooded rulers out there in the setting who have a massive harem comparable to that of a Khan or an Egyptian Pharaoh and who are trying to have as many children as possible with their mortal spouses in the hopes that some of their children will Exalt, because they don't know the ins and outs of Terrestrial Exaltation and doesn't realize that they need a set period of time in between having children.<br /> <br /> That's presumably not going to happen in the Realm or Lookshy or Prasad, because those kingdoms are probably more aware of some of the aspects of Exaltation and over the centuries (or through looking at Shogunate era material) realize that, to a degree, the longer one waits in between having children the more likely the child is to Exalt. But many of the Lost Eggs and Outcastes in Creation probably don't have that sort of &quot;meta&quot; knowledge about their Exaltation.<br /> <br /> In the end what's important, of course, is that while a Dragon Blooded might <i>try</i> to sire or give birth to a legion of Dragon Blooded, that simply isn't something he or she can actually accomplish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T22:21:06-08:00","id":1171458,"title":"","content":"Ehhh this feels like a solution to a \u201cproblem\u201d that really wasn\u2019t. Why don\u2019t DBs optimize their fucking for quality and quantity of offspring? Because they\u2019re <i>people</i>, and <i>seriously who does that?!</i> I mean you have the Ottoman Sultans, sure, but their approach to inheritance led to a system where every single potential heir had to be a cutthroat survivor, because once an heir was named, all the other candidates were -ceremonially murdered to prevent a succession crisis. If you want a legion of demigods, that ain\u2019t how you get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T00:28:15-08:00","id":1171476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171415#post1171415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's something the devs explained thoroughly; even Dragon-Blooded can't just crank out hundreds of Dragon-Blooded babies. The best chances they have at their kids Exalting is when there's years and years between conceiving said kids.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So...what's the official canon on the official numbers right from the beginning then?<br /> <br /> How fecund is House Cathak in this sense?<br /> <br /> Why did the refractory period take so long?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21242-charonferryman","name":"CharonFerryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T01:58:20-08:00","id":1171485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CharonFerryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171476#post1171476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So...what's the official canon on the official numbers right from the beginning then?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was 5000 years ago. Who knows. <br /> Certainly there wasn't 100 male DBs and 9900 female DBs who spent the first few years of the war being pregnant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How fecund is House Cathak in this sense? </div> </div> </div>As fecund as any other house? I'm not really understanding this question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why did the refractory period take so long? </div> </div> </div>Because the magic takes a long time to regenerate.<br /> <br /> (I mean, actually it's to explain demographics and shut up the arguments about why DBs don't have breeding farms)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T02:09:03-08:00","id":1171487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171410#post1171410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honest question: how would this ever work in actual play? Are timeskips of multiple decades really all that frequent in Exalted chronicles? My personal experience is that real downtime is rare and mostly means either a few days to a few weeks in transit (depending mainly on whether someone took Stormwind Rider) or maybe a few months for the season to change, so I'd think that the story would be largely <i>over </i>by the time you see any kind of return on investment for these Charms. Maybe it could work if the group starts out playing older Lunars, but 1) again, IME, that rarely happens, and 2) it would only work for justifying merits purchased at chargen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a timeskip of 26 years. Two moon-touched beastmen children (one sharkman, one orang-utan girl) of Lunar PCs grew up, teamed up, and went and shouted at the Full Moons for being terrible parents.<br /> <br /> But, honestly, you're largely right. We have a moon-touched NPC attached to our party, as I mentioned. He's less than 2 years old. So not very useful. Though if there'd been a charm to give your kids cool mutations (like exalted healing!), I suspect his mum's player would have taken them before giving birth.<br /> <br /> Tbh, they'd be the sort of charms that only occasionally are useful for PCs, but they'd be useful for NPCs. It'd give STs an idea of what kind of things they can do with mad Lunar kings in the threshold and their beastmen hordes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-29-2017, 07:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T04:42:45-08:00","id":1171505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171485#post1171485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was 5000 years ago. Who knows.<br /> Certainly there wasn't 100 male DBs and 9900 female DBs who spent the first few years of the war being pregnant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm..then I have a harder time believing that there are legions of DBs during the First Age.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As fecund as any other house? I'm not really understanding this question. </div> </div> </div>From 2E<br /> <br /> <i>Famed as one of the most militaristic of the Great Houses, House<br /> Cathak has been blessed by the Dragons with a better Exaltation<br /> rate than any House but Mnemon\u2019s. Even more auspiciously, House<br /> Cathak has produced more children than any other Great House<br /> for 80 out of the last 100 years. For other Great Houses, this would<br /> be a blessing. For House Cathak, it\u2019s necessary to offset the House\u2019s<br /> equally high mortality rate. The majority of young Cathaks (Exalted<br /> or not) enter the legions, where they strive to equal or surpass the<br /> legends of the House\u2019s great war heroes\u2014and the House\u2019s casualty<br /> rate reflects that. More tragedies befall the young soldiers of this Great<br /> House than any other. Publicly, this is attributed to the fearlessness<br /> of House Cathak. Privately, it is often claimed that, while members<br /> of the House are long on bravery, they\u2019re short on judgment. Some<br /> members even secretly claim that it\u2019s an extravagant conspiracy<br /> engineered by Mnemon to keep House Cathak from taking control of<br /> the Dynasty simply by outbreeding the rest of the Great Houses.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because the magic takes a long time to regenerate.<br /> <br /> (I mean, actually it's to explain demographics and shut up the arguments about why DBs don't have breeding farms) </div> </div> </div>That won't cut the arguments about breeding farms. It can still be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21242-charonferryman","name":"CharonFerryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T05:29:11-08:00","id":1171510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CharonFerryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171505#post1171505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That won't cut the arguments about breeding farms. It can still be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I fail to see why the lack of breeding farms needs any explanation beyond &quot;<i>Dude.</i>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T06:25:20-08:00","id":1171517,"title":"","content":"We know that mortals with terrestrial heritage get a small but static chance of producing dragonblooded kids. Under the new system if you want to generate a lot of DBs quickly they might be a safer bet. <br /> <br /> And this is fine because as we all know, mortals aren't people. /sarcasm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T06:50:00-08:00","id":1171521,"title":"","content":"Even setting aside questions about breeding farms, a lot about the subject of Dragon Blooded reproduction has always been vague in a way that was not helpful when it's an important subject about their lifestyle and politics. For instance, there would be a few places saying that, on average, a couple might have one child every 12 years and maybe have something like ten children ever, but there was never really anything that laid down how many of these children would actually Exalt.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo the concept of progenitive Essence can help clarify that if, as I suspect it will, the answer will be &quot;for two well-bred Exalted, basically all of their children can be expected to Exalt, but only if they wait a decent amount of time between children&quot;. It makes a significant aspect of their society a lot less muddy, which will probably help with playing in that setting and devising character backgrounds.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt also plays into some of their adjustments to the gender dynamics of Dynast society, such as the attitude toward extramarital children.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for the First Age, I have a suspicion that the current writers aren't quite as big on the idea of there being <i>so</i> many of them as there were in Second Edition, but assuming at least a notion that there were more than ten thousand, I would say that can be chalked up to living longer with the aid of anagathics, more of them being able to have children as a result of a somewhat safer world, and maybe some additional mystical resources to help reduce the downtime.<br /> <br /> \u200bBecause the idea of progenitive Essence is not the only thing they're using to add a bit more consistency to Dragon Blooded numbers; Eric has consistently made comments suggesting to me that there's going to be a bit more emphasis on the mortality rate that prevents many from having children at all, as well as frequently cleaning out the prior generations.<br /> <br /> That's another side to it; you don't need to treat people like brood mares in order for a population of people with significantly higher lifespans to explode over time, because population is a matter of both birth and death rate. Even if we assumed that Dragon Blooded had no more children than the average modern Western person, and did so between about the same ages, you're still dealing with the fact that if they keep living for centuries afterwards, then the population is going to keep growing and growing. That is, after all, a very significant part of the population explosion from the 19th century onwards; improved medicine, nutrition and living conditions allowing more people to live longer. Just look at a picture of a family tree going back over a couple of centuries, and imagine if <i>all</i> of those people were still alive, and multiply it by several dozen families.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Age of Sorrows becomes a bit unwieldy if there are too many Dragon Blooded around, so adding new elements and emphasizing old ones behind keeping it relatively compact has its uses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T07:02:25-08:00","id":1171523,"title":"","content":"I think there was some notion somewhere that during the Great Contagion dragonblooded numbers got as low as a thousand or so, and they've been steadily climbing back ever since.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T12:48:24-08:00","id":1171596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171523#post1171523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there was some notion somewhere that during the Great Contagion dragonblooded numbers got as low as a thousand or so, and they've been steadily climbing back ever since.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably from one of GCG's old quotes about what actually keeps the Fair Folk back (not even 3000 Terrestrials with access to power armor and Gundams, it turns out; just the RDG, but I think everyone probably knows that by now).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T14:25:22-08:00","id":1171624,"title":"","content":"Actually it works quite well to explain why they needed it <i>then</i> but haven't had to use it for years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T20:27:36-08:00","id":1171703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171521#post1171521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even setting aside questions about breeding farms, a lot about the subject of Dragon Blooded reproduction has always been vague in a way that was not helpful when it's an important subject about their lifestyle and politics. For instance, there would be a few places saying that, on average, a couple might have one child every 12 years and maybe have something like ten children ever, but there was never really anything that laid down how many of these children would actually Exalt.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo the concept of progenitive Essence can help clarify that if, as I suspect it will, the answer will be &quot;for two well-bred Exalted, basically all of their children can be expected to Exalt, but only if they wait a decent amount of time between children&quot;. It makes a significant aspect of their society a lot less muddy, which will probably help with playing in that setting and devising character backgrounds.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt also plays into some of their adjustments to the gender dynamics of Dynast society, such as the attitude toward extramarital children.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for the First Age, I have a suspicion that the current writers aren't quite as big on the idea of there being <i>so</i> many of them as there were in Second Edition, but assuming at least a notion that there were more than ten thousand, I would say that can be chalked up to living longer with the aid of anagathics, more of them being able to have children as a result of a somewhat safer world, and maybe some additional mystical resources to help reduce the downtime.<br /> <br /> \u200bBecause the idea of progenitive Essence is not the only thing they're using to add a bit more consistency to Dragon Blooded numbers; Eric has consistently made comments suggesting to me that there's going to be a bit more emphasis on the mortality rate that prevents many from having children at all, as well as frequently cleaning out the prior generations.<br /> <br /> That's another side to it; you don't need to treat people like brood mares in order for a population of people with significantly higher lifespans to explode over time, because population is a matter of both birth and death rate. Even if we assumed that Dragon Blooded had no more children than the average modern Western person, and did so between about the same ages, you're still dealing with the fact that if they keep living for centuries afterwards, then the population is going to keep growing and growing. That is, after all, a very significant part of the population explosion from the 19th century onwards; improved medicine, nutrition and living conditions allowing more people to live longer. Just look at a picture of a family tree going back over a couple of centuries, and imagine if <i>all</i> of those people were still alive, and multiply it by several dozen families.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Age of Sorrows becomes a bit unwieldy if there are too many Dragon Blooded around, so adding new elements and emphasizing old ones behind keeping it relatively compact has its uses.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think this, together with the clarification of marriages, are some examples of trying to dig too deep ends up creating a larger hole than intended.<br /> <br /> Because just as easily someone could ask why isn't the Left Hand of Power more involved in the aftermath of the Great Contagion/Balorian Crusade, especially if the Bronze Faction is so desperate to shore up Creation's last line of defense that the Left Hand would have to play a far larger role and therefore obtain greater political and spiritual power instead of being so diminished? Why would he even need to constantly petition the Greater Elemental Dragons if he was already running an eugenics program currently? Why would he not be able to influence the refractory period of this progenitive Essence?<br /> <br /> Again, these questions will keep on coming. Sometimes I do wonder if digging so deep is actually helpful or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21242-charonferryman","name":"CharonFerryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T20:47:24-08:00","id":1171708,"title":"","content":"When did we get any word on Parad's political status in Third Edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T21:02:58-08:00","id":1171717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171708#post1171708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When did we get any word on Parad's political status in Third Edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ask the Devs has it a few times. <br /> Parsaad is a satrapy, but its an exception to a lot of the satrapy rules do to sheer distance. It's also the crown jewel of the Realm's satrapies I believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T21:43:02-08:00","id":1171730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171708#post1171708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When did we get any word on Parad's political status in Third Edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>July, 2017. <a href=\"http://read:http://theonyxpath.com/the-realm-preview-exalted/\" target=\"_blank\">The Realm Preview about Prasad</a>. It may be hard to read at the moment, due to the 'snowflake' script chewing up resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T23:22:46-08:00","id":1171743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CharonFerryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171505#post1171505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> That won't cut the arguments about breeding farms. It can still be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it really can't. Not in the conditions implied by the term &quot;breeding farm&quot;. In 3E canon, to maximize efficiency in producing the greatest possible number of Dragon-Blooded offspring, you need to wait 15 years between each conception for female and male Dragon-Blooded alike. &quot;Breeding Farm&quot; implies a population kept captive to be used for nothing but breeding. That doesn't work with the required gap. Not in anyway that makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T23:30:45-08:00","id":1171744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171458#post1171458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehhh this feels like a solution to a \u201cproblem\u201d that really wasn\u2019t. Why don\u2019t DBs optimize their fucking for quality and quantity of offspring? Because they\u2019re <i>people</i>, and <i>seriously who does that?!</i> I mean you have the Ottoman Sultans, sure, but their approach to inheritance led to a system where every single potential heir had to be a cutthroat survivor, because once an heir was named, all the other candidates were -ceremonially murdered to prevent a succession crisis. If you want a legion of demigods, that ain\u2019t how you get it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can think off the top of my head of dozens of cases of societies that put huge social effort on maximizing reproduction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T00:51:10-08:00","id":1171748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171744#post1171744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I can think off the top of my head of dozens of cases of societies that put huge social effort on maximizing reproduction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and how many of those put people in breeding camps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T00:55:50-08:00","id":1171749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171743#post1171743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it really can't. Not in the conditions implied by the term &quot;breeding farm&quot;. In 3E canon, to maximize efficiency in producing the greatest possible number of Dragon-Blooded offspring, you need to wait 15 years between each conception for female and male Dragon-Blooded alike. &quot;Breeding Farm&quot; implies a population kept captive to be used for nothing but breeding. That doesn't work with the required gap. Not in anyway that makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If the idea of progenitive essence is still valid, and the fact that DB blood can lie dormant even in non-DBs, just keep breeding. Those that don't exalt now can still produce children that Exalt later.<br /> <br /> Once everyone starts passing around, eventually the overall frequency of Exalting will increase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21242-charonferryman","name":"CharonFerryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T01:15:07-08:00","id":1171750,"title":"","content":"Persons, Sunder is not asking about Prasad the semi-satrapy in the southeast, but Parad, god of inherited power, the Left Hand of Power to Lytek's Right.<br /> <br /> I propose that adding him to this equation from out of nowhere is kind of going off half-cocked with assumptions and looking for things to complain about, which might finally truly elevate him to Lytek's status.<br /> <br /> I presume that he has little real power to upset the dynamic as the developers have presented it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T07:47:29-08:00","id":1171788,"title":"","content":"*deleted because misunderstood original statement*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 12-30-2017, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T09:26:18-08:00","id":1171808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171750#post1171750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Persons, Sunder is not asking about Prasad the semi-satrapy in the southeast, but Parad, god of inherited power, the Left Hand of Power to Lytek's Right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T12:32:50-08:00","id":1171857,"title":"","content":"This is third edition. If you are making assumptions about the (canon) setting not a) backed by a statement in 3rd edition materials or b) backed by a statement from a dev, you're already building on a foundation of ice, not stone. And given the amount of &quot;back to First Edition&quot; involved in the setting development, if you are citing something from 2e alone, the ice is quite thin.<br /> <br /> As far as the war against the Primordials, not only that but the whole First Age is explicitly being put behind a veil of ignorance and legend for 3rd. How many DBs were there for the war, and how were they created? This is not known, and (barring a change of heart on the part of the dev team) will not be answered. The war was thousands of years ago; the game line is focused on the current day.<br /> <br /> And whether breeding camps were ever realistic or not, they are now, as a practical matter, impossible. You could, from the information we currently have, at best infer that you could manage to make a mortal population as likely to produce Dragon-Blooded as the Realm's patrician class. But even that <i>assumes</i> that mass breeding of DBs to mortals automatically upgrades the kids' chances regardless of the state of the DB's progenerative essence, which is not a given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T13:42:46-08:00","id":1171878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CharonFerryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171749#post1171749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If the idea of progenitive essence is still valid, and the fact that DB blood can lie dormant even in non-DBs, just keep breeding. Those that don't exalt now can still produce children that Exalt later.<br /> <br /> Once everyone starts passing around, eventually the overall frequency of Exalting will increase.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've only been on board with Exalted, both the game and the community, since Ex3, so I don't have the baggage on this breeding farm argument.<br /> <br /> But holy shit, it is exasperating.<br /> <br /> In what world does this make sense? You have to raise a child for 12-18 years, before you even know you got what you wanted. The best way to do it is to get a revolving door of demigod couples to bang, the woman go through the pregnancy and then just give you their child. That is to have the best chance, and this same couple can't do it for 12-20 years, if I'm not mistaken.<br /> <br /> The you gotta raise potential demigod children so that if, and thats a big if, they actually become demigods they don't hate you and try to destroy you. And then they Exalt. Yay great! Now what? They are demigods, they have their own passions, goals, and most importantly power.<br /> <br /> How does a person fit this into &quot;breeding farm&quot;? This is one of the most aggravating relics of the previous edition, its probably the saddest remnant of terrestrials suckszors out there. If you have the kind of power to get a &quot;breeding farm&quot; of dragonbloods going, what the hell you need dragonbloods for. Just own the setting with that power and thats it, move to another game.<br /> <br /> Sorry for ranting, but this is tiring and tired subject. I know I shouldn't have got into this discussion, but with the DB books on the horizon I had hope that DBs would get more Elemental Superhero discussion than nonsensical rape and slavery allusion. Of Exalted.<br /> <br /> C'mon people, DBs are EXALTED. They own the setting. They are not cattle, and no ranch would exist capable of turning them into such. Its like saying you want to set up a breeding farm of geniuses, of gifted athletes, of amazing artists. You can't control for shit like this, even if genetics are a component of it. And it doesn't make any business sense either. What kind of objectibe even requires this? If you have power and resources to pull this off, you can invest that power to get almost anything else in the setting...<br /> <br /> There I go ranting again, after already apologizing for it... I'm off now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T03:38:13-08:00","id":1171985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171878#post1171878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've only been on board with Exalted, both the game and the community, since Ex3, so I don't have the baggage on this breeding farm argument.<br /> <br /> But holy shit, it is exasperating.<br /> <br /> In what world does this make sense? You have to raise a child for 12-18 years, before you even know you got what you wanted. The best way to do it is to get a revolving door of demigod couples to bang, the woman go through the pregnancy and then just give you their child. That is to have the best chance, and this same couple can't do it for 12-20 years, if I'm not mistaken.<br /> <br /> The you gotta raise potential demigod children so that if, and thats a big if, they actually become demigods they don't hate you and try to destroy you. And then they Exalt. Yay great! Now what? They are demigods, they have their own passions, goals, and most importantly power.<br /> <br /> How does a person fit this into &quot;breeding farm&quot;? This is one of the most aggravating relics of the previous edition, its probably the saddest remnant of terrestrials suckszors out there. If you have the kind of power to get a &quot;breeding farm&quot; of dragonbloods going, what the hell you need dragonbloods for. Just own the setting with that power and thats it, move to another game.<br /> <br /> Sorry for ranting, but this is tiring and tired subject. I know I shouldn't have got into this discussion, but with the DB books on the horizon I had hope that DBs would get more Elemental Superhero discussion than nonsensical rape and slavery allusion. Of Exalted.<br /> <br /> C'mon people, DBs are EXALTED. They own the setting. They are not cattle, and no ranch would exist capable of turning them into such. Its like saying you want to set up a breeding farm of geniuses, of gifted athletes, of amazing artists. You can't control for shit like this, even if genetics are a component of it. And it doesn't make any business sense either. What kind of objectibe even requires this? If you have power and resources to pull this off, you can invest that power to get almost anything else in the setting...<br /> <br /> There I go ranting again, after already apologizing for it... I'm off now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You have nothing to apologize for - I get that you find this weird, but then again... this is exalted. In first age Solars and Lunars would 'ski' down mountains on tyrant lizards, just for fun.<br /> <br /> And your point about 'dormant' dragonblood is exactly why I figured that a Lunar could shapeshift into someone with that and then pass it around. It's been canon for quite a while that some Lunars set themselves up as local gods to tribes or smalls communities - combine that with some 2nd ed breeding charms (basically to ensure 100% chance of conception) and oh hey, maybe word spreads that everyone who prays to this god and gets a 'visit' from said sexy deity has a much higher than average chance of having their child exalt as a DB.<br /> <br /> The thing about Lunar breeding programs, and the Thousand Streams projects, is that they tend to be long term programs - and why would a DB want a string of tribes or a city state on the edge of creation to have a sudden increase in DBs? Could be to ward off a Fair Folk threat that'll come knocking in 20 years, could be to strengthen some nearby not-realm-allied warlords. Who knows.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T09:03:08-08:00","id":1172011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171985#post1171985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You have nothing to apologize for - I get that you find this weird, but then again... this is exalted. In first age Solars and Lunars would 'ski' down mountains on tyrant lizards, just for fun.<br /> <br /> And your point about 'dormant' dragonblood is exactly why I figured that a Lunar could shapeshift into someone with that and then pass it around. It's been canon for quite a while that some Lunars set themselves up as local gods to tribes or smalls communities - combine that with some 2nd ed breeding charms (basically to ensure 100% chance of conception) and oh hey, maybe word spreads that everyone who prays to this god and gets a 'visit' from said sexy deity has a much higher than average chance of having their child exalt as a DB.<br /> <br /> The thing about Lunar breeding programs, and the Thousand Streams projects, is that they tend to be long term programs - and why would a DB want a string of tribes or a city state on the edge of creation to have a sudden increase in DBs? Could be to ward off a Fair Folk threat that'll come knocking in 20 years, could be to strengthen some nearby not-realm-allied warlords. Who knows.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, don't get me wrong, I understand why someone would want MOAR DBS any place, really.<br /> <br /> I just don't get how &quot;breeding farm&quot; is the way to go, given the specifics of the situation. If you have 20 years notice on a Fair Folk raid, you are going to get one cycle of reproduction&gt;maturity, so how many dormant db people you would have to maintain for decades and how many 20 year old DBs you're gonna get back from that? How many are gonna stay once they Exalt and can escape?<br /> <br /> With all those resources can't you create an awesome manse, found an order, create powerful Artifacts, make it the seat of power in the region and offer all that to a DB family to take over and be protectors of the land or some shit?<br /> <br /> I mean there are many incentives to colonize places. We should take a cue from the real world. Where in the history of humanity did someplace keep human presence by dint of there being a breeding program there? When empires wanted to conquer and colonize they offered, opportunity to those willing to go. Opportunity to gain wealth, more freedoms, social climbing, evasion of punishment, etc...<br /> <br /> No place was colonized by slaves. Slaves are brought either to fight or to labor, they are never the foundation.<br /> <br /> If you want DBs somewhere you gotta give them reasons and incentives to be and stay there, they are Exalted. Like someone said upthread, the Realm is a perfect example of an organization trying to maximize the number of DBs in their midst. They are Royalty. They have all these perks. They have control. <br /> <br /> That is the kind of physical and social infrastructure required to attempt something like this, for it to be a cohesive program.<br /> <br /> You can have thousands of dormant DB mortals breeding for centuries and not get a single Exaltation. Meanwhile you're feeding, keeping generally healthy, at least minimally satisfied with their lot, thousands of people, for howerver long it lasts. And if you luck out and get a few DBs out of it, whats keeping them there?<br /> <br /> I just don't see it working under the vision of this edition of the game. Mind whammies are much less prevalent, the Dragonblooded Exaltation has retaken the mystique and power that it is owed, and is not simply a matter of genes and breeding anymore. I think we could do the DBs, actually the whole gameline, a service and not try to reduce them to that again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T10:36:01-08:00","id":1172026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171985#post1171985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You have nothing to apologize for - I get that you find this weird, but then again... this is exalted. In first age Solars and Lunars would 'ski' down mountains on tyrant lizards, just for fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see a pair playing Initial Dinosaur once, but its novelty probably wore off rather quickly. Also, it doesn't really have much bearing on trying to instate breeding programs for Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And your point about 'dormant' dragonblood is exactly why I figured that a Lunar could shapeshift into someone with that and then pass it around. It's been canon for quite a while that some Lunars set themselves up as local gods to tribes or smalls communities - combine that with some 2nd ed breeding charms (basically to ensure 100% chance of conception) and oh hey, maybe word spreads that everyone who prays to this god and gets a 'visit' from said sexy deity has a much higher than average chance of having their child exalt as a DB. </div> </div> </div>No, not even in 2e could Lunars manage this. Their Dragon-Blooded forms were still just as Dragon-Blooded as they were, which is to say, not at all unless they had the Terrestrial Bloodline merit. Which they would not have from Essence 4 on, and had only the most meager of chances to produce Dragon-Blooded offspring. You're way better off using your store of spare faces to play people against each other. The only suggestion for a Charm required you to actually pair with Dragon-Blooded, and was also non-canonical, strictly speaking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing about Lunar breeding programs, and the Thousand Streams projects, is that they tend to be long term programs - and why would a DB want a string of tribes or a city state on the edge of creation to have a sudden increase in DBs? Could be to ward off a Fair Folk threat that'll come knocking in 20 years, could be to strengthen some nearby not-realm-allied warlords. Who knows.<br /> </div> </div> </div>The other thing about them is that they really just didn't work. Nothing in the 2e Lunars book worked; its factions were painfully artificial, the stated purpose meandered around and didn't really have a clear goal, and all of the elders acted like they were from V:tM. This was a canard from late 1e that didn't do the Lunars any favors. That's presumably part of the reason why it's going, going, gone. It's out of here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T12:29:16-08:00","id":1172046,"title":"","content":"Ugh, yeah, the factions really were quite artificial. &quot;This faction has spent 1500 years telling young Lunars to obey their Solar mates. Even though everyone thought the Solars were never coming back.&quot; &quot;This Lunar faction thinks fighting the Raksha is really important. And... so do all the other Lunars actually. So basically this faction is just Lunars who live near the Wyld.&quot; &quot;This Lunar faction is the No Moon faction. They're No Moons. They do No Moon stuff. As you'd expect from No Moons.&quot; &quot;This Lunar faction loves nature! That's basically it.&quot; &quot;This Lunar faction thinks the Thousand Streams are great. And... so do all the other Lunars actually.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not sure the writers really understood how games of political intrigue work.<br /> <br /> Or how the social organisation of 300 people across an entire planet would work.<br /> <br /> I'm not against the idea of Lunar groupings and societies per-se, they just needed far more thought. (The Silver Pact as an organisation of some but not all Lunars makes more sense.)<br /> <br /> So, yeah, glad that's gone.<br /> <br /> I'm sure all the weird Werewolf social stuff about Renown that was in 2nd ed Lunars will be gone too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T13:29:46-08:00","id":1172059,"title":"","content":"I'd expect Lunars to have developed a bit of a bronze/gold split of their own. Those who are happy to see the solars back and those who blame them for the current mess, maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T14:26:31-08:00","id":1172071,"title":"","content":"YesI can see that.<br /> <br /> But it has only been five years (and in the first year, a lot of Lunars probably didn't know/believe the Solars had returned), so it's probably not at the level of &quot;factions&quot; so much as arguments. And, of course, it's happening in real time, with Solars doing their thing too; there's already going to be Lunars working with Solars, Lunars fighting Solars, Lunars avoiding Solars, Lunars eating Solars and impersonating them, etc, even while the elders argue about it. Unlike the Sidereals, who have 80-ish members working down the road from each other, the Lunars are solo or in small clumps all across the world. So even as Lunars debate with each other about whether the Silver Pact itself should ally with the Solars or not, individual Lunars are already going to have taken a variety of action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T19:52:12-08:00","id":1172137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1172071#post1172071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">YesI can see that.<br /> <br /> But it has only been five years (and in the first year, a lot of Lunars probably didn't know/believe the Solars had returned), so it's probably not at the level of &quot;factions&quot; so much as arguments. And, of course, it's happening in real time, with Solars doing their thing too; there's already going to be Lunars working with Solars, Lunars fighting Solars, Lunars avoiding Solars, Lunars eating Solars and impersonating them, etc, even while the elders argue about it. Unlike the Sidereals, who have 80-ish members working down the road from each other, the Lunars are solo or in small clumps all across the world. So even as Lunars debate with each other about whether the Silver Pact itself should ally with the Solars or not, individual Lunars are already going to have taken a variety of action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Sidereals tend toward the calm and contemplative, whereas a major part of what motivates Lunars is RAGE! Also, a taste for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=f4Mc-NYPHaQ\" target=\"_blank\">freedom from old legacies</a>, but being denied that so often, it tends to be RAGE!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T22:41:22-08:00","id":1172191,"title":"","content":"The one relationship that's not on the cards, as per the 3e core, is going back to being the Solars' seconds, as they were in the First Age; as Saur Ops says, they've got a taste for freedom from old legacies...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T15:46:18-08:00","id":1172410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1172059#post1172059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd expect Lunars to have developed a bit of a bronze/gold split of their own. Those who are happy to see the solars back and those who blame them for the current mess, maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does 3rd have Sun King Seneschals? In 2nd there was a faction of lunars were solar fanboys - but nothing official about any groups who were decidedly anti-solar or anything","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T17:30:17-08:00","id":1172455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1172410#post1172410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does 3rd have Sun King Seneschals? In 2nd there was a faction of lunars were solar fanboys - but nothing official about any groups who were decidedly anti-solar or anything</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't expect any parts of 2e Lunar society to show up in 3e, because, as has been mentioned, they didn't work or make sense, and weren't really reflective of how people act in the slightest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T04:54:49-08:00","id":1172609,"title":"","content":"They exist but it's like three of them and they haven't seen one member in months.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T06:55:11-08:00","id":1172628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1172455#post1172455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't expect any parts of 2e Lunar society to show up in 3e, because, as has been mentioned, they didn't work or make sense, and weren't really reflective of how people act in the slightest.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I dunno - even with that new lunar island place and whatnot, then an informal group of &quot;wouldn't it be nice with the solars came back&quot; Lunars would still fit into the lore IMO.<br /> <br /> Sure, there'd probably also be an informal group of &quot;Oh hell no those assholes just kicked us around all day&quot; Lunars","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T07:31:08-08:00","id":1172634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1172628#post1172628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno - even with that new lunar island place and whatnot, then an informal group of &quot;wouldn't it be nice with the solars came back&quot; Lunars would still fit into the lore IMO.<br /> <br /> Sure, there'd probably also be an informal group of &quot;Oh hell no those assholes just kicked us around all day&quot; Lunars</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that many Lunars will have strong feelings about the return of the Solars, and some of those feelings will be &quot;aw HELL yeah, my best buddy is back and we are gonna GET SHIT DONE&quot;, but calling those collective sentiments a 'Faction' might be too strong a word.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T09:10:13-08:00","id":1172658,"title":"","content":"Yes, the Sun King Seneschals would have made more sense as something called a faction if they were something like a group dedicated to figuring out what had happened to the Solars and hastening their return, and agitating for other Lunars to do the same, but as it was they were apparently just the people who were most sad about the Solars being gone.<br /> <br /> \u200bLeviathan, I think, was often referred to as being among the most prominent of the Seneschals, and what did that amount to? How he had a hobby of personally and brutally murdering any Terrestrial Exalted who happened to pop up in his domain?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, there'd probably also be an informal group of &quot;Oh hell no those assholes just kicked us around all day&quot; Lunars</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI mean, there's probably a Lunar, or some of them, who have such a bad experience with their own Solars. I still think Lilith's story has a place in the setting, so long as it's <i>hers</i> rather than a major definition of the Lunar experience, and also if it's not gone into too much detail.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor the rest, the Third Edition core has established a line in which Lunars with reservations about the returning Solars have reasons a bit more complex than the Solars mistreating them.<br /> <br /> Although I'd say the main thing that is being established from the outset is that these are feelings that are being grappled with by every Lunar individually, rather than it being something that is drawing battle lines in the group.<br /> <br /> \u200bThink about it, even if one was to decide that there are, say, twenty or thirty Lunars who, for one reason or another, have responded to the return of the Solars with a sentiment of &quot;I'm okay with, or even enthusiastic about, this&quot;, calling them a group creates this impression of them having gotten together and doing something about it, which seems impractical with their current setup.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm all for the Lunars book discussing the idea for player or non-player characters (including dimensions where such decisions are being made for characters who have and have not already met Solars in general or ones with whom they have history specifically), but it shouldn't be phrased in terms of them being a group.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T09:48:45-08:00","id":1172666,"title":"","content":"Okay, now I can see where the tangent about Lunar factions came in...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171985#post1171985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And your point about 'dormant' dragonblood is exactly why I figured that a Lunar could shapeshift into someone with that and then pass it around. It's been canon for quite a while that some Lunars set themselves up as local gods to tribes or smalls communities - combine that with some 2nd ed breeding charms (basically to ensure 100% chance of conception) and oh hey, maybe word spreads that everyone who prays to this god and gets a 'visit' from said sexy deity has a much higher than average chance of having their child exalt as a DB.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI mean, it's also generally been canon that people with really insignificant Dragon Blooded lineage have basically no chance of Exalting, so I'm not sure where you're getting this idea of a noticeable increase in the odds or the numbers from just one Lunar is coming from.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat you seem to be saying is that if a Lunar shapeshifts into, say, a Dynast's mortal great-grandchild (what I assume you mean by &quot;dormant Dragon Blood&quot;) they can go around the Threshold impregnating children, and that will have a noticeable effect on Dragon Blooded population. And the only advantage that they have over an actual mortal doing this is conception rates of 100%, as opposed to what they would be for a normal person (which aren't necessarily low).<br /> <br /> \u200bThe setting just does not remain consistent if you assume that something like this would work. You don't even need breeding camps for it; several thousand mortal Dynasts going on holiday in areas with significant numbers of sexually available women would have at least the same effect.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat does having a higher than average chance even mean in this context? After all, it could be that the chance of having one's child Exalt rises from 1 in 5 million to 1 in 1 million, which would make the statement both accurate and actually constitute a significant increase in the odds, while the chance still amounts to basically zero, and being largely unrecognisable besides.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about Lunar breeding programs, and the Thousand Streams projects, is that they tend to be long term programs</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWith regard to this, being a long term project would need to be the kind of thing where your results build upon one another, something complicated by how much this particular plan hinges upon producing people who will eventually die. If you spend a thousand years spreading a thin bit of Dragon Blood around and have ten Exalted children to show for it (three of whom died of old age since you started), that's not a long term project, that's just a thing that you've been doing for ages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">why would a DB want a string of tribes or a city state on the edge of creation to have a sudden increase in DBs? Could be to ward off a Fair Folk threat that'll come knocking in 20 years, could be to strengthen some nearby not-realm-allied warlords. Who knows.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOkay, here you're talking about the motivations of some DB, but I don't know who they're supposed to be (you make a comment there implying that they're not supposed to be from the Realm), so I don't really understand this statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T16:01:17-08:00","id":1172779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1172658#post1172658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the Sun King Seneschals would have made more sense as something called a faction if they were something like a group dedicated to figuring out what had happened to the Solars and hastening their return, and agitating for other Lunars to do the same, but as it was they were apparently just the people who were most sad about the Solars being gone.<br /> <br /> \u200bLeviathan, I think, was often referred to as being among the most prominent of the Seneschals, and what did that amount to? How he had a hobby of personally and brutally murdering any Terrestrial Exalted who happened to pop up in his domain?</div> </div> </div> </div>And if we're going back to first edition Leviathan, we're getting someone who ultimately gave no fucks about the Solars and who didn't have a Solar superior in the First Age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T17:09:06-08:00","id":1172806,"title":"","content":"When it comes to the subject of character reproduction, I think I can see a few things moving away from anything that would so much as hint at the viability of going around sewing your wild oats as widely as possible, whether they're just a matter of common characterisation, or the actual functionality of things. For instance, given some of the history of Lunars and their children, I really like how the corebook opted to re-introduce the idea of Lunars having empowered beastfolk children by giving the example of the three daughters of a particular Lunar, who are all given actual names and distinct personalities; it gives me the impression of trying to condition us to tell stories about something more focused and personal, rather than the presumed subservience of a massive cast of nameless, faceless descendants. This might be something reinforced when the Lunars book ultimately codifies the developer statement that the association between those Exalted and societies of beastfolk is more a matter of employing their powers to transform people, then having sex with them and coming back a few hundred years later when the animal genes have propagated through several thousand people.<br /> <br /> \u200bSimilarly, when it comes to the question of Dragon Blooded eugenics (which is foremost a concern for the actual Dragon Blooded rather than a single given Lunar who might be able to approximate or appropriate that lineage, and thus needs to consider how it would work for large numbers of them), I propose that in addition to the limited Essence, good breeding might be something that entails a complex combination of a large number of characteristics. That might mean that it needs to be honed down to the individual and calculation of some other individual who might have maximum compatibility, which would both prevent it from becoming too expansive, and create an avenue for drama in the form of needing to ensure that people who are biologically compatible for the Essence taking in their offspring are also interpersonally compatible. I think this would be both logically consistent with the setting as it has usually been portrayed and the details being added, and shift focus away from the Dragon Blooded community being a vast machine of interchangeable parts.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat all touching upon how, even at the best of times, a given Lunar would still be an outsider to this whole process.<br /> <br /> \u200bHell, I can actually see a process by which the idea of a Lunar, or anybody else, introducing Dragon Blood into a community might work; maybe I'm just not reading other posts closely enough and they're actually saying what I am, but I at least think that the conclusions are a bit different, since I'm seeing a process that would technically work, but would be functionally absurd.<br /> <br /> \u200bBecause it would be one in which it's not enough for the Dragon Blooded progenitor to go around impregnating large numbers of women; that would introduce the necessary bloodline, but in the first generation it would probably be so insignificant as to never result in Exaltation for anybody, and thereafter becomes increasingly less pronounced unless you're also exerting control over who your children are reproducing with (setting aside the unpleasant matter of how you might be maximizing your results if you ensure that they have children with one another). That might not be a level of control over what is presumably a widely dispersed population that is beyond one of the Exalted, but apart from the difficulty of doing so discretely when both the Dragon Blooded and the Lunars have powerful figures seeking to regulate them, it strikes me as just, well... tedious.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's really a thing with a lot of these fantasy or science fiction shadowy, manipulative Methusalehs; that their renditions of mysterious long term projects are so often portrayed as completely inscrutable to outsiders would often strike me as the kind of thing that is not really generating any short term results at all, which raises questions about how one can maintain investment in it, and whether or not the opportunity cost it represents might be better spent elsewhere. In some properties, that might work if you can credibly portray the manipulator as inhumanly patient enough to be so dedicated, but that's not really a mindset that I find consistent with the Exalted. Not to say that none of them are patient, just that I couldn't really buy any of them going in for a plan that would consist of tedious routine over the course of centuries that ultimately achieves a result, as opposed to a consistent series of short term gains and accomplishments that build upon one another to achieve a long term goal. It's how the plan of the Silver Pact works, after all.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhen it comes down to it, a Lunar who wants some Dragon Blooded children is probably best off finding a willing Exalt to settle down with and raising somewhere between two and four of them, focusing more on the specific, surgical goals that those people might accomplish as lone operators or a well-coordinated team, rather than trying to outdo the Realm as a whole. I warrant it makes for a more interesting and stirring story and all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T14:04:56-08:00","id":1173079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1172666#post1172666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, now I can see where the tangent about Lunar factions came in...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, it's also generally been canon that people with really insignificant Dragon Blooded lineage have basically no chance of Exalting, so I'm not sure where you're getting this idea of a noticeable increase in the odds or the numbers from just one Lunar is coming from.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat you seem to be saying is that if a Lunar shapeshifts into, say, a Dynast's mortal great-grandchild (what I assume you mean by &quot;dormant Dragon Blood&quot;) they can go around the Threshold impregnating children, and that will have a noticeable effect on Dragon Blooded population. And the only advantage that they have over an actual mortal doing this is conception rates of 100%, as opposed to what they would be for a normal person (which aren't necessarily low).<br /> <br /> \u200bThe setting just does not remain consistent if you assume that something like this would work. You don't even need breeding camps for it; several thousand mortal Dynasts going on holiday in areas with significant numbers of sexually available women would have at least the same effect.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat does having a higher than average chance even mean in this context? After all, it could be that the chance of having one's child Exalt rises from 1 in 5 million to 1 in 1 million, which would make the statement both accurate and actually constitute a significant increase in the odds, while the chance still amounts to basically zero, and being largely unrecognisable besides.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bWith regard to this, being a long term project would need to be the kind of thing where your results build upon one another, something complicated by how much this particular plan hinges upon producing people who will eventually die. If you spend a thousand years spreading a thin bit of Dragon Blood around and have ten Exalted children to show for it (three of whom died of old age since you started), that's not a long term project, that's just a thing that you've been doing for ages.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bOkay, here you're talking about the motivations of some DB, but I don't know who they're supposed to be (you make a comment there implying that they're not supposed to be from the Realm), so I don't really understand this statement.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) You can have very pure dragonblood and not exalt - that'll more than open you up to a celestial exaltation<br /> 2) I was thinking, if a Lunar was going &quot;Ok, so if this huge swath of Creation is going to get rekt because I can't hold back all these Raksha. How about I tweak things by adding some stronger dragonblood to the local populace, so a few more DBs will exalt in the region. Hopefully they'll want to defend their homeland too&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T14:23:27-08:00","id":1173085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1173079#post1173079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 1) You can have very pure dragonblood and not exalt - that'll more than open you up to a celestial exaltation</div> </div> </div> </div>No it won't. Case in point: most mortal Dynasts don't end up as the other classic Exalted, and their lineage is typically quite &quot;pure&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) I was thinking, if a Lunar was going &quot;Ok, so if this huge swath of Creation is going to get rekt because I can't hold back all these Raksha. How about I tweak things by adding some stronger dragonblood to the local populace, so a few more DBs will exalt in the region. Hopefully they'll want to defend their homeland too&quot; </div> </div> </div>The other part of the GCG quote about 3000 Terrestrials in Gundams being chaff before the Fair Folk hordes was that thousands more Terrestrials with imperishable k-bars wouldn't fare any better. Also, the Fair Folk were broken after the Empress used the RDG, to the point where they would never be an existential threat to Creation ever again, and Creation was no longer shrinking, so the plans would have all circled back to &quot;kill the Realm&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T14:31:30-08:00","id":1173086,"title":"","content":"You know, quoting an entire sizable post like that creates a bit of ambiguity about what exactly it is that you're responding to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1173079#post1173079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 1) You can have very pure dragonblood and not exalt - that'll more than open you up to a celestial exaltation</div> </div> </div> </div>That's accurate, but I don't see the relevance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) I was thinking, if a Lunar was going &quot;Ok, so if this huge swath of Creation is going to get rekt because I can't hold back all these Raksha. How about I tweak things by adding some stronger dragonblood to the local populace, so a few more DBs will exalt in the region. Hopefully they'll want to defend their homeland too&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis sentence in particular is hard to tell what it's actually responding to, but I can still say that the general sentiment is begging the question of how a Lunar who wants this thing can meaningfully accomplish it.<br /> <br /> Also &quot;hopefully they'll want to take part&quot; is a terribly lax attitude towards protecting the world, don't you think?<br /> <br /> \u200bNever mind whether or not a specific Lunar has any distinctly better ability to add more Dragon Blooded to a sizable region than the actual Dragon Blooded of the Realm do, what you're describing just sounds like a very slipshod kind of agenda.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T15:42:25-08:00","id":1173100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1171195-lunar-dragon-blooded-breeding?p=1171200#post1171200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately (well, maybe fortunately for the setting), it doesn't work.<br /> Lunars can take the form of Dragonblood, but they don't gain the Dragonblood exaltation. So just as they don't gain the Dragonblood's charms, they don't gain the Dragonblood's ability to create Dragonblooded kids. They just don't have the magic necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct. The Dragon's blood is part of the miracle of Exaltation, not a mundane genetic marker; you can't replicate it with magic.<br /> <br /> (Obviously, feel free to continue discussing the consequences of house rules to the contrary! Just clarifying about the line's official stance.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}